If you're reading this, I will be or am already dead by suicide. I think anyone who cares deserves an explanation. Please let me explain.

I was born on May 26th, 2002, in Vynetsia, Ukraine. I was then adopted by my parents, Brad and Mary Jane Henderson. My mom and dad had unrealistic expectations of what having a child was like, and I was punished my whole life for that. My parents sent me to psychiatrists because when I was younger I didn't follow directions. I was put on medication, which is one of the biggest reasons I am dead or soon will be; psychiatric drugs kill millions, but I will explain and provide evidence for that later.

In high school, I had a 4.1 GPA, and my parents did the three things that led to my death. The first was not letting me go into AP classes. I can remember having close to a religious experience by the washing machine when, after pleading with my parents to sign the form, they said no. My faith in education and institutions was destroyed then, and at that point, it was further destroyed by everything after.

The second was not getting me a car when I was 16. I wanted to become financially independent, but getting a job is impossible without a car (my parents don't believe this very obvious, true fact).

The third thing my parents did that led to my death was preventing me from going to the colleges I wanted to go to. I was given a choice of three schools even though I could have possibly gotten into Columbia, NYU, Cornell, or many other very good schools that would have provided an edge in the absurd capitalist job market.

At 24, with a physics degree, no car, and 900+ job applications with no response, the future that I predicted has come true. I can't even get hired at Dunkin' Donuts.

As for psychiatry, they are equally to blame as my parents. Psychiatry is built on a Western lie: that human psychological suffering is medical. It is not and never will be the case. They commit violence that kills people. My best friend also died the same way I did on September 3rd. https://macfaddenfuneralhome.com/tribute/details/1203/Joseph-Phillips-V/obituary.html

Look, obviously everyone involved in this doesn't know any better. My parents don't know any better, and neither do the psychiatrists. But what people need is not complicated. They need community, good material conditions (transportation, housing, food, disposable income, etc.), and they need meaningful relationships, both romantic and platonic.

We live under a mode of production where my friend and I were deprived of some of these things at every turn of our existence. I tried really hard to change my material conditions, but I can't. My parents refuse to even get me an $800 car when they live in a big house in North Carolina that they bought in cash.

Please don't blame yourself. Just please honor me by taking care of one another and abolishing psychiatry.

Look, there is no easy solution to the problems humanity is facing. The only thing you can really do is love everyone. It is crucially important that we love our enemies and that we see the humanity in our ideological and political opponents. Recognizing each other's personhood and suffering is the only way we can survive.

I love you all,

Chris Henderson
